   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "If…",
     "texto": [
      "The ending **-(으)면** presents a condition or a general situation: 가다 → **가면** (if I go), 먹다 → **먹으면** (if I eat), 있다 → **있으면** (if there is/you have), 좋다 → **좋으면** (if the weather is good / if it is good). Depending on context it can also be translated as «when»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How it is formed",
     "texto": [
      "After a vowel you add **-면**; after another consonant, **-으면**. With stems ending in **ㄹ**, use **-면** and keep the ㄹ: 살다 → **살면**, 만들다 → **만들면**.",
      "시간이 **있으면** 같이 가요 = if you have time, let's go together."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
